<td id="A1.T4.3.5.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_b ltx_border_r ltx_border_t"><math id="A1.T4.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{d}m+hm" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{d}m+hm</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A1.T4.3.5.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_b ltx_border_r ltx_border_t"><math id="A1.T4.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{d}h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{d}h</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="A1.T4.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 4</span>. </span><span id="A1.T4.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">GEMM operations’ FLOPs and memory access in a decode batch.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A1.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For the attention operation, we discuss the attention operation with FlashAttention <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">Dao et al., 2022</a>)</cite> optimization. Given a request with <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> prompt tokens, inputs <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐐</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Q}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐊</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{K}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{V}\in\mathbb{R}^{p\times s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{V}\in\mathbb{R}^{p\times s}</annotation></semantics></math>, the attention computation is expressed follows:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{S}=\mathbf{Q}\mathbf{K}^{\top}\in\mathbb{R}^{p\times p},\mathbf{P}=\text{softmax}(\mathbf{S})\in\mathbb{R}^{p\times p},\mathbf{O}=\mathbf{P}\mathbf{V}\in\mathbb{R}^{p\times s}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐒</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>𝐐𝐊</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝐏</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>softmax</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐒</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝐎</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐏𝐕</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{S}=\mathbf{Q}\mathbf{K}^{\top}\in\mathbb{R}^{p\times p},\mathbf{P}=\text{softmax}(\mathbf{S})\in\mathbb{R}^{p\times p},\mathbf{O}=\mathbf{P}\mathbf{V}\in\mathbb{R}^{p\times s}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">We refer to the forward pass algorithm 2 in FlashAttention <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">Dao et al., 2022</a>)</cite> for the following IO operation analysis. First, every K, V block is loaded only once from HBM to SRAM, which counts for <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2sp" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2sp</annotation></semantics></math> memory read access. For each K, V block pair, the corresponding Q, O blocks need to be loaded, performing the attention computation, and write back to O. This accounts for the addition of <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2sp" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2sp</annotation></semantics></math> memory read access and <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="sp" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">sp</annotation></semantics></math> memory write access. Rather than operating on each individual K,V pair, FlashAttention operated on blocks of K, V pairs with block size <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math>. The total number of K, V block pairs can be expressed as <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p/b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p/b</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, the total memory access for prefill with prompt token length <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2sp+3sp\cdot(p/b)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2sp+3sp\cdot(p/b)</annotation></semantics></math>. For flops computations, the multiplication of the matrix of <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="QK^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">QK^{T}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="PV" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">PV</annotation></semantics></math> yields <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2p^{2}s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2p^{2}s</annotation></semantics></math> flops.
Therefore, together with the GEMM computation and memory access, the computation and memory access of a batch with <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{p}</annotation></semantics></math> prefill requests can be represented as:</p>
<table id="A1.E6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A1.E6X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_left">(6)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E6X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle M_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle M_{p}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E6X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=4h^{2}+8\sum\limits_{i=0}^{B_{p}-1}p_{i}h+2hm+2tm+2sp+3sp\cdot\frac{p}{b}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>p</mi><mi>b</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=4h^{2}+8\sum\limits_{i=0}^{B_{p}-1}p_{i}h+2hm+2tm+2sp+3sp\cdot\frac{p}{b}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E6Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E6Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle F_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle F_{p}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E6Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=4\sum\limits_{i=0}^{B_{p}-1}p_{i}h^{2}+2\sum\limits_{i=0}^{B_{p}-1}p_{i}hm+2p^{2}s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=4\sum\limits_{i=0}^{B_{p}-1}p_{i}h^{2}+2\sum\limits_{i=0}^{B_{p}-1}p_{i}hm+2p^{2}s</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.3. </span>Decode Analysis</h3>

<div id="A1.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Similarly, for decode analysis, we also first consider GEMM operations. The computational flops and the memory access of the GEMM operations are presented in Table <a href="#A1.T4" title="Table 4 ‣ A.2. Prefill Analysis (w.o chunking) ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ Ascendra: Dynamic Request Prioritization for Efficient LLM Serving" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>.
For the attention operation of decode, assuming a request with 1 prefill token only, to decode the first token, the related <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k,v\in R^{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mi>s</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k,v\in R^{s}</annotation></semantics></math> of the first token needs to be fetched along with the query vector <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q\in R^{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mi>s</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q\in R^{s}</annotation></semantics></math>; for the second generated token, we need to fetch the <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k,v\in R^{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mi>s</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k,v\in R^{s}</annotation></semantics></math> of the first generated token as well as the second query vector <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q\in R^{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mi>s</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q\in R^{s}</annotation></semantics></math>, etc. Therefore, to generate <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> tokens, it requires <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3sp" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3sp</annotation></semantics></math> memory access. However, this only holds true if there is only one decoding request in a batch and the total number of prefill token and decode token does not exceed the SRAM capacity.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">To generalize this, we consider the batched scenario in which multiple decode requests exist. Their memory may exceed the SRAM capacity. Thus, to decode a single token from a request, one may need to reload <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k,v\in R^{p\times s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k,v\in R^{p\times s}</annotation></semantics></math> of the prefilled prompt as well as the previously generated tokens into SRAM. In such a scenario, the memory access during decode attention depends on the number of requests in the current batch as well as their individual related <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K,V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K,V</annotation></semantics></math> size. However, we can derive an upper bound of this memory access.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Assuming that for every decoding token of a request, we need to reload the <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k,v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k,v</annotation></semantics></math> of its prefilled prompt as well as all tokens generated up to now. For a request <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{l}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>l</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{l}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> prefill tokens and generated tokens, the memory access of all decoding request in this batch is bounded by
<math id="A1.SS3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum\limits_{i=0}^{i=B_{d}-1}2\hat{l}_{i}s+2s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></munderover><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>l</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum\limits_{i=0}^{i=B_{d}-1}2\hat{l}_{i}s+2s</annotation></semantics></math>,
where 2s represents the <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k,v\in R^{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mi>s</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k,v\in R^{s}</annotation></semantics></math> for the generated token.
For the flops computation of the decode batch, the new query vector <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q\in R^{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mi>s</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q\in R^{s}</annotation></semantics></math> needs to compute its attention against all prefill and generated <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k,v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k,v</annotation></semantics></math>, which can be expressed as
<math id="A1.SS3.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum\limits_{i=0}^{i=B_{d}-1}2\hat{l}_{i}s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></munderover><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>l</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum\limits_{i=0}^{i=B_{d}-1}2\hat{l}_{i}s</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Therefore, together with the GEMM computation and memory access, the computation and memory access of a batch with <math id="A1.SS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> decode requests can be represented as:</p>
<table id="A1.E7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A1.E7X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_left">(7)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E7X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle M_{d}=4h^{2}+8Bh+2hm+2Bm+\sum\limits_{i=0}^{i=B_{d}-1}2\hat{l}_{i}s+2s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>l</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle M_{d}=4h^{2}+8Bh+2hm+2Bm+\sum\limits_{i=0}^{i=B_{d}-1}2\hat{l}_{i}s+2s</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E7Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E7Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle F_{d}=4Bh^{2}+2Bhm+\sum\limits_{i=0}^{i=B_{d}-1}2\hat{l}_{i}s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>l</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle F_{d}=4Bh^{2}+2Bhm+\sum\limits_{i=0}^{i=B_{d}-1}2\hat{l}_{i}s</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.4. </span>Hybrid Batch with Chunked Prefill</h3>

<div id="A1.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In a hybrid batch with chunked prefill, the GEMM operations if the prefill request and decode requests can be derived from table <a href="#A1.T3" title="Table 3 ‣ A.2. Prefill Analysis (w.o chunking) ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ Ascendra: Dynamic Request Prioritization for Efficient LLM Serving" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>&amp; <a href="#A1.T4" title="Table 4 ‣ A.2. Prefill Analysis (w.o chunking) ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ Ascendra: Dynamic Request Prioritization for Efficient LLM Serving" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> individually. Similarly, the memory access and flops calculation for the deoding request still is bounded by the result derived in <a href="#A1.SS3" title="A.3. Decode Analysis ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ Ascendra: Dynamic Request Prioritization for Efficient LLM Serving" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.3</span></a>. However, the memory access for the chunked prefill requests is closely related to the number of processed prompt tokens of each request up to the current batch.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Suppose that there are <math id="A1.SS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{p}</annotation></semantics></math> prefills in a hybrid batch. The total number of prefill tokens processed in the batch can be expressed as
<math id="A1.SS4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum\limits_{i=0}^{B_{p}-1}c_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum\limits_{i=0}^{B_{p}-1}c_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>.
To compute the attention for prompt chunk of each request in the current batch, we need to load all previously processed <math id="A1.SS4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k,v\in R^{l\times s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k,v\in R^{l\times s}</annotation></semantics></math> of each request in the current batch. This accounts for <math id="A1.SS4.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2l_{i}s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2l_{i}s</annotation></semantics></math> memory access for each request. Similarly to <a href="#A1.SS2" title="A.2. Prefill Analysis (w.o chunking) ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ Ascendra: Dynamic Request Prioritization for Efficient LLM Serving" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.2</span></a>, for every <math id="A1.SS4.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k,v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k,v</annotation></semantics></math> block pair, we need to load the <math id="A1.SS4.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math> block to compute the attention. However, the difference from <a href="#A1.SS2" title="A.2. Prefill Analysis (w.o chunking) ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ Ascendra: Dynamic Request Prioritization for Efficient LLM Serving" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.2</span></a> is that we only need to access the <math id="A1.SS4.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math> block of the current chunk. The total memory access for each <math id="A1.SS4.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k,v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k,v</annotation></semantics></math> block pair is <math id="A1.SS4.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3c_{i}s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3c_{i}s</annotation></semantics></math>, which accounts for the memory read, write for the <math id="A1.SS4.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q,o" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>o</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q,o</annotation></semantics></math> block. The total number of <math id="A1.SS4.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k,v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k,v</annotation></semantics></math> block pairs is equal to <math id="A1.SS4.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l_{i}/b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l_{i}/b</annotation></semantics></math>. So the memory access of the prefill tokens in the current hybrid batch is expressed as
<math id="A1.SS4.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum\limits_{i=0}^{B_{p-1}}2l_{i}s+3c_{i}s(l_{i}/b)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></munderover><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum\limits_{i=0}^{B_{p-1}}2l_{i}s+3c_{i}s(l_{i}/b)</annotation></semantics></math>. Regarding the count of flops, the query <math id="A1.SS4.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q\in R^{c_{i}\times s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q\in R^{c_{i}\times s}</annotation></semantics></math> in the current batch of request <math id="A1.SS4.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> needs to perform attention against all previous processed <math id="A1.SS4.p2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K,V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K,V</annotation></semantics></math> tokens of <math id="A1.SS4.p2.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. The amount of flops in <math id="A1.SS4.p2.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P=qK^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P=qK^{T}</annotation></semantics></math> can be expressed as <math id="A1.SS4.p2.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="sl_{i}c_{i},q\in R^{c_{i}\times s},K\in R^{l_{i}\times s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mrow><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">sl_{i}c_{i},q\in R^{c_{i}\times s},K\in R^{l_{i}\times s}</annotation></semantics></math>, and in <math id="A1.SS4.p2.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O=PV" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O=PV</annotation></semantics></math> can be expressed as <math id="A1.SS4.p2.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="sl_{i}c_{i},P\in R^{c_{i}\times l_{i}},V\in R^{l_{i}\times s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mrow><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">sl_{i}c_{i},P\in R^{c_{i}\times l_{i}},V\in R^{l_{i}\times s}</annotation></semantics></math>. So, to prefill all query tokens for request <math id="A1.SS4.p2.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> in the current batch, the total flops can be expressed as <math id="A1.SS4.p2.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2sl_{i}c_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2sl_{i}c_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. So in a hybrid batch with <math id="A1.SS4.p2.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{p}</annotation></semantics></math> chunked prefill requests, the flops count can be expressed as
<math id="A1.SS4.p2.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum\limits_{i=0}^{B_{p}-1}2sl_{i}c_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum\limits_{i=0}^{B_{p}-1}2sl_{i}c_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Together with the decode request <math id="A1.SS4.p2.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> in the batch, we express the total memory access in the hybrid batch as</p>
<table id="A1.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle M_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle M_{m}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=4h^{2}+2hm+\Bigg(8\sum\limits_{i=0}^{B_{p-1}}l_{i}h+2\sum\limits_{i=0}^{B_{p-1}}l_{i}m+\sum\limits_{i=0}^{B_{p-1}}2l_{i}s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=4h^{2}+2hm+\Bigg(8\sum\limits_{i=0}^{B_{p-1}}l_{i}h+2\sum\limits_{i=0}^{B_{p-1}}l_{i}m+\sum\limits_{i=0}^{B_{p-1}}2l_{i}s</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(8)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\quad+3c_{i}s\frac{l_{i}}{b}\Bigg)+\Bigg(8B_{d}h+2B_{d}m+\sum\limits_{i=0}^{B_{d}-1}2\hat{l}_{i}s+2s\Bigg)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>b</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>l</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad+3c_{i}s\frac{l_{i}}{b}\Bigg)+\Bigg(8B_{d}h+2B_{d}m+\sum\limits_{i=0}^{B_{d}-1}2\hat{l}_{i}s+2s\Bigg).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The corresponding flops can be expressed as</p>
<table id="A1.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle F_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle F_{m}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\Bigg(\sum\limits_{i=0}^{B_{p}-1}\big(4c_{i}h^{2}+2c_{i}hm+2sl_{i}c_{i}\big)\Bigg)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\Bigg(\sum\limits_{i=0}^{B_{p}-1}\big(4c_{i}h^{2}+2c_{i}hm+2sl_{i}c_{i}\big)\Bigg)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(9)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\quad+\Bigg(4B_{d}h^{2}+2B_{d}hm+\sum\limits_{i=0}^{B_{d}-1}2\hat{l}_{i}s\Bigg)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>l</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad+\Bigg(4B_{d}h^{2}+2B_{d}hm+\sum\limits_{i=0}^{B_{d}-1}2\hat{l}_{i}s\Bigg).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.5. </span>Goodput Comparison</h3>

<div id="A1.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><a href="#A1.F14" title="Figure 14 ‣ A.5. Goodput Comparison ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ Ascendra: Dynamic Request Prioritization for Efficient LLM Serving" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure 14</span></a> shows the goodput performance of models on different datasets that is not presented in the main paper.</p>
</div>
